Add graceful shutdown with in-flight request draining to this worker pool, preserving the existing cancellation semantics and without introducing deadlocks:
```go
type Pool struct {
    jobs    chan Job
    wg      sync.WaitGroup
}
func (p *Pool) Start(n int) {
    for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
        p.wg.Add(1)
        go func() {
            defer p.wg.Done()
            for job := range p.jobs {
                job.Run()
            }
        }()
    }
}
func (p *Pool) Submit(j Job) {
    p.jobs <- j
}
```
Callers currently call `Submit` from many goroutines concurrently and expect it to never block indefinitely once shutdown begins; a job already running must be allowed to finish, but no new jobs should start.

